{
  "name": "Chat with PDF, Word and PowerPoint files using Apify and OpenAI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Chat with PDF, Word and PowerPoint files using Apify and OpenAI\n\n### Who's it for\nTeams and builders who want a Q&A assistant over their own documents (handbooks, contracts, reports, course material) with answers that cite the file and page.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Add documents form**: paste links to PDF, Word, PowerPoint or Excel files.\n2. **Convert to Markdown chunks** runs the **Document to Markdown for AI & RAG** Actor on Apify. It keeps headings and tables, runs OCR on scanned PDFs and splits each file by heading into chunks with page numbers.\n3. **Prepare chunks** keeps the text plus source file, page and heading as metadata.\n4. **Store chunks** embeds them with OpenAI and saves them in a vector store.\n5. In the **Chat**, the **Document assistant** searches the chunks and answers with the source file and page.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Create a **Header Auth** credential named `Apify API token`: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN` (Apify Console \u2192 Settings \u2192 API & Integrations).\n2. Add your OpenAI credential to the three OpenAI nodes.\n3. Open the form URL, add links, then open the chat.\n\n### Requirements\nAn Apify account and an OpenAI API key. Files must be reachable by URL (public or shared links). Cost on Apify: about $0.002 per page, plus $0.005 per scanned page with OCR.\n\n### How to customize\nChange chunk size and OCR in **Settings**. The in-memory vector store is for testing: swap **Store chunks** and **Search documents** for Pinecone, Qdrant, Supabase or PGVector in production.",
        "height": 960,
        "width": 600,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "3bdbbda8-cd52-497f-b890-97bdfceb3bc0",
      "name": "Template description",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        80
      ]
    },
